WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:01.770
We have a voicemail number.

00:00:01.770 --> 00:00:06.830
That number is two one nine two David P. I
don't know if this voicemail is for real or

00:00:06.830 --> 00:00:08.931
not, but let's take a listen to it.

00:00:08.931 --> 00:00:10.780
It's about Bernie's three houses.

00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:12.269
Hi David.

00:00:12.269 --> 00:00:14.710
It's calling from [inaudible].

00:00:14.710 --> 00:00:17.960
Sorry, it's calling from Washington state.

00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:22.189
I had a question about Bernie Sanders.

00:00:22.189 --> 00:00:28.189
Uh, my dad who listens to conservative radio
all the time.

00:00:28.189 --> 00:00:36.649
He claims that Bernie raised a lot of money
outside of, of, uh, selling his book and he's

00:00:36.649 --> 00:00:39.010
got like three houses or something.

00:00:39.010 --> 00:00:40.010
Okay.

00:00:40.010 --> 00:00:43.059
Possibly make a big deal on that and clear
that out.

00:00:43.059 --> 00:00:47.150
So I don't know that I believe, you know,
three houses or something.

00:00:47.150 --> 00:00:52.109
I don't know that I believe this is a sincere
voicemail, but let's, let's see if we can

00:00:52.109 --> 00:00:54.489
desegregate this.

00:00:54.489 --> 00:00:57.270
Bernie did not raise money by selling a book.

00:00:57.270 --> 00:01:01.710
Bernie wrote a book and that's a commercial
endeavor and he made money from selling it

00:01:01.710 --> 00:01:05.480
several, many hundreds of thousands of dollars
as would be expected from a politician of

00:01:05.480 --> 00:01:08.910
his stature and notoriety in society.

00:01:08.910 --> 00:01:15.980
Bernie raised money for his campaign from
individuals and uh, Bernie does have three

00:01:15.980 --> 00:01:16.980
houses.

00:01:16.980 --> 00:01:20.300
And what matters is that Bernie wants health
care for everybody.

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:24.960
Bernie wants higher taxes on the very rich
to pay for things that would benefit all of

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:27.080
society, so on and so forth.

00:01:27.080 --> 00:01:31.470
Bernie's net worth of, I believe it was one
point $1 million is not at all outrageous

00:01:31.470 --> 00:01:35.840
for a guy who's nearly 80 years old and has
made six figures for quite some time now as

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:39.650
an elected official at the top level in the
United States.

00:01:39.650 --> 00:01:44.460
And my instinct is that this is concerned
fake concern trolling.

00:01:44.460 --> 00:01:49.990
Um, but if it's a serious question, no, you
don't have to be worried about that.

00:01:49.990 --> 00:01:54.850
Go by the policies and then you will very
quickly see when you compare Bernie Sanders

00:01:54.850 --> 00:02:00.100
to Donald Trump or to Joe Biden whose policies
would be best for the greatest number of people.

